/**
@page debug Debugging

@c bnt_debug.h adds per-header logging helpers on top of a backend. Include it
after the backend header.

@section debug_printk Trace output

Each header type has a @c __printk helper that writes the header's fields to the
kernel trace pipe, read with @c cat @c /sys/kernel/debug/tracing/trace_pipe:

@code{.c}
#include "bnt_xdp.h"
#include "bnt_debug.h"

bnt_eth eth;
if (!bnt_eth__parse(ctx, 0, &eth))
    bnt_dbg_eth__printk(&eth);
@endcode

@section debug_events Structured events

Each header type also defines a typed event struct, @c bnt_dbg_<type>_event, and
three helpers that produce it:

- @c __fill_event populates the struct from a view.
- @c __emit_ringbuf submits one event to a ring buffer.
- @c __update_map stores the latest event under a map key.

A ring buffer streams every event to user space; a map keeps only the most recent
event per key. Numeric event fields are in host byte order, except addresses,
which keep their network-order on-wire form.
*/
